		高压力睡眠碎片化: "🚑 Core recommendation:\nRelieve stress to improve sleep\n🩺 Analysis hint:\n“High stress levels may cause you to wake easily at night and experience fragmented sleep, reducing sleep quality.”\n💉 Specific suggestions:\n1. Pre-sleep relaxation: try in-app breathing guides (e.g., 4-7-8 breathing) or mindfulness meditation.\n2. Reduce night-time disturbances: limit fluids before bed and ensure the bedroom is quiet.\n3. Daytime stress management: cultivate hobbies, talk with family and friends, and seek professional psychological support if needed.",
		高疲劳睡眠时长不足: "🚑 Core recommendation:\nPrioritize catching up on sleep\n🩺 Analysis hint:\n“We have detected high fatigue and insufficient sleep recently, the main causes of daytime drowsiness and low energy.”\n💉 Specific suggestions:\n1. Set a bedtime reminder: go to bed 30-60 minutes earlier than usual.\n2. Create a wind-down ritual: avoid blue-light devices one hour before bed; read or listen to soft music instead.\n3. Avoid excessive weekend catch-up: wake up no more than one hour later than usual to prevent circadian disruption.",
		高疲劳深睡比例异常: "🚑 Core recommendation:\nIncrease sleep depth\n🩺 Analysis hint:\n“Your total sleep time is adequate, but deep sleep is insufficient, so your body and brain do not fully recover.”\n💉 Specific suggestions:\n1. Regular exercise: perform at least 30 minutes of daytime aerobic activity (e.g., brisk walking, jogging), but avoid vigorous exercise within three hours of bedtime.\n2. Optimize the sleep environment: keep the bedroom completely dark and cool (18-22 °C).\n3. Avoid pre-sleep stimulants: no caffeine, alcohol, or large meals after dinner.",
